# Server credentials = confidential, kahin bhi share nahi

**Hard rule (user ka instruction):** Server ke credentials confidential hain — **kahin bhi, kisi se bhi share nahi karne**.

## Confidential kya hai
- SSH host / IP / port / username / private key path ya key content
- Hosting account ID, hPanel login, API tokens
- DB host / database name / DB username / DB password
- `.env` ki koi bhi value (`APP_KEY`, `DB_*`, `MAIL_*`, API keys), `bootstrap/cache/config.php`
- Server paths jo account ID reveal karein

## Kahan kabhi nahi jaana chahiye
- **Git / repo** (repo PUBLIC hai): code, docs, `PROJECT_STANDARDS.md`, `.cursor/rules/*`, tests, commit messages, PR descriptions
- **Chat replies / summaries** — user ko bhi values dobara print mat karo; sirf "`DEPLOY.local.md` mein hai" bolo
- **Logs / error output / screenshots** — commands ka output secrets print kare to aisa command mat chalao (`cat .env`, `env`, `config:show database`, etc.)
- **Third-party / external services**: web search, WebFetch, pastebins, issue trackers, external APIs
- **Subagents / Task prompts** — credentials subagent prompt mein mat daalo
- Client-side JS, Blade output, PDFs, emails

## Allowed
- Server details sirf `DEPLOY.local.md` (gitignored) mein; secrets sirf server ki `.env` (600) mein
- SSH commands chalana jab task ko zaroori ho — bina secrets print kiye (`stat`, `grep -c`, status codes)
- Commit/push se pehle: `git diff --cached` mein IP, account ID, DB name, passwords, keys grep karo

## Agar galti se leak ho jaye
- Turant user ko batao (kya, kahan), push ho chuka ho to rotation recommend karo — chhupao mat
